#!parity-excluded harness: `bench` block — the bench runner prints elapsed wall-clock time into stdout
# CoW view-materialization on the BENCH body-lowering path.
#
# AXIS CELL — `bench` bodies (`lower_bench_items`, src/ir/lowering/mod.rs). The
# fourth and last of the module-loop paths (setup / teardown / test are in
# `cow_test_body_view_survives_realloc.gg`), and one of eleven
# function-body-lowering paths. Like its three siblings it ran a HAND-COPIED
# SUBSET of the per-function prescans — liveness only — so
# `cow_reassigned_after` was empty, the element view stayed a lazy borrow, and
# the 64 pushes reallocated it away. Only `gg test --bench` lowers this body.
#
# THE REALLOC IS LOAD-BEARING (64 pushes), and the payload is heap-FORCED via
# `mk` so ASan reports a legible heap-use-after-free, not a bare SIGSEGV.
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the pre-fix compiler: `gg test --bench` died with SIGSEGV.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

bench "view bound in a bench body survives a realloc":
    Vector[String] v = [mk("hello", "world")]
    String s = v.get(0).unwrap()
    int i = 0
    while i < 64:
        v.push(mk("xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx", "yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy"))
        i = i + 1
    print(s)
